[Music]  adventure hound reckless goofball big  grin not the brightest bob in the box  these are the descriptors that  immediately come to mind when you think  about monkey d luffy but occasionally  our childlike hero and pirate  extraordinaire does something so crazily  awesome you realize there's more to him  than meets the eye he demands your  respect and admiration and you give it  gladly when it comes to ability and  sheer pluck luffy's got it all he might  not think things through and might get  his crewmates in a tough spot more than  once because of his impulsiveness but  he's also innately kind just brave and  generous he's got all the qualities of a  hero and when he shows this side of his  character the only way to describe him  is badass paying tribute to these heroic  quantities here are the top 10 badass  luffy moments in one piece  at number 10 luffy shows us what a  terrifying monster he can be by knocking  out 50 000 fish man pirates with his  conquerors haki while luffy used this  unique form of haki which only a chosen  few can wield on several occasions  throughout the series his display on  fishman island is amongst the most  memorable it's not just the numbers he  defeats but also his prowess at using  this god-given power the slack-jawed  look of shock and surprise on hodi's  face says all there is to say of the  impact luffy has on the enemy's morale  with this show of strength luffy's  actions have an immediate and deep  impact while his battle with hody goes  the whole hog and even gives him some  trouble this early moment shows that  luffy's victory is but inevitable  [Music]  next up is luffy one shotting bellamy in  the gyre arc  before his rather unexpected and moving  character progression in the dress  russell arc benemi's a small time thug  whose arrogance cynicism and all-round  bad behavior make him insufferable he's  called bellamy the hyena and he lives up  to his nickname emulating the animal's  physical features and opportunistic  tendencies in jaya bellamy picks a fight  with luffy in a bar when luffy in a rare  show of maturity refuses to engage in a  meaningless brawl bellamy beats up and  humiliates the straw hat captain and  zorro but nobody beats up luffy and gets  away with it it's just not done bellamy  gets his comeuppance when luffy one  shots him in the middle of town knocking  him out cold and shutting him up for  good right in the middle of his springy  dance it's an intensely satisfying punch  one that even saitama would be proud of  coming in at number eight is luffy's  revelation of gear fourth bound man  well it's a pleasure to watch luffy go  from strength to strength with each gear  fourth gear is the most visually  arresting of the lot in the bruising  battle against don quixote doflamingo  luffy goes into gear forth by biting  down on his forearm and inflating his  body with air to resemble a giant  balloon while also enhancing his muscle  strength the transformation is dramatic  as it is but series creator ichiro oda  makes it even more fantastic with the  addition of some kabuki style theatrics  in the fight luffy uses the fourth gear  technique bound man which allows him to  bounce up and down and gain incredible  speed and power it's the perfect counter  to dophie who's no lightweight in the  power department  [Applause]  [Music]  for the next badass moment we have luffy  doing what he does best making a  spectacle of himself in the most  unconventional manner  the watershed battle of marineford to  save ace from being executed by the  marines begins in earnest when luffy  falls from the sky from an upturned boat  a bunch of rag tag allies on his heels  the sight of luffy and his noisy crew  free-falling into the fight arena sends  shockwaves throughout the marines and  pirates down below considering how the  battle ends this entrance is both  comical and irreverent the complete  opposite of whitebeard's epic entrance a  little earlier in the day the  lightheartedness of it all prevents any  foreshadowing of the darkness and  tragedy that's just about to come in  fact luffy brings with him a sense of  hope that all will be well but despite  everything that happens luffy's grand  entrance can never be forgotten  [Music]  at number six we have luffy  sucker-punching kaido in his dragon form  in their very first meeting in muano  if there's anything luffy excels at it's  being impulsive and doing the opposite  of what he should be doing after the  lord luffy alliance arrives in wano the  strategy they adopt is to keep a low  profile and work in secrecy to bring  down the yonko but their plans go up in  smoke as luffy not only reveals himself  to kaido in a fit of rage but also  chases him down and lands a punch on him  powerful enough to slam him senseless  into the ground troop kaido is drunk as  a skunk when he's bought down by a  single hit to the head but the fact that  kaido is in his dragon form at this  moment is a testimony to luffy's power  and bravado it also raises the  anticipation sky high for the duo's  final clash which should definitely be  worth the wait  in the fifth spot is luffy using  conquerors haki during the battle of  marineford  as the executioner's blades come down on  ace and the situation looks dire luffy  unleashes this incredible power failing  the killers of most of the pirates and  marines this haki display is totally  different from the one of fishman island  for one luffy's actions in marineford  are unconscious born out of desperation  to save his brother even as those around  him are stunned luffy is completely  unaware of what he's done secondly he  manages to subdue a much more powerful  crowd compared to the fishman pirates  the marineford gang is made up of some  of the fiercest pirates and toughest  marines it's safe to say this is the  moment luffy officially announces his  arrival in the new world  [Music]  next up is luffy declaring war on the  world government in ennis lobby  the ark to rescue robin from the cp9 a  group of assassins on the government's  payrolls is one of the most heartfelt in  the entire series it really captures the  spirit of the theme of nakama that runs  through one piece like blood in the  veins usop in his so gay king disguise  puts in an mvp performance as he on  luffy's orders shoots down the world  government symbol of power its flag with  a fiery slingshot the burning flag is a  burning example of just how far luffy  and his crew are willing to go for one  of their own and for what they believe  to be just and right this moment comes  early in the series but it's such a  powerful one it can't be forgotten in a  hurry  number three is luffy facing off against  the three admirals in the marineford arc  which as you would have realized by now  is a minefield of impactful moments  the three admirals aokiji akainu and  kizaru are the true symbols of the  navy's power each gifted with the devil  fruit power so mighty that they're a  threat to the fiercest pirates going up  against even one of them could mean  certain defeat maybe even death and yet  luffy is neither afraid nor hesitant  when he pole vaults his way to get in  their collective face he's clearly  exhausted from fighting his way through  weak from the sea water and desperate to  save ace but his glaring eyes show no  fear on the other hand the terror on  aces face makes it all too clear what  great danger luffy might have landed  himself in thanks to this poster worthy  moment we can't wait for that inevitable  final clash between luffy and the  marines top brass  [Music]  in the runner-up spot is luffy  challenging big mom for the second time  [Music]  isn't the kind of woman you make an  enemy of even by accident she not only  has one of the most fearsome devil fruit  powers she's also extremely cruel  tyrannical and unpredictable luffy who  knows no fear has had a hostile  relationship with her from the get-go he  first picks a fight with her without  ever having laid eyes on her but it's  his second challenge that leaves all  witnesses to the seed including the  yonko herself speechless this one too  like the first one takes place over den  den denmushi captured and jailed on  whole cake island luffy not only mocks  big mom for her controlling ways and her  ambition of becoming the king of pirates  but he also vows to take back sanji and  have the last laugh in their contest  from how it looks it's clearly a case of  an ant challenging an elephant the look  of outrage and incredulous belief on big  mom's face says it all  [Music]  punching its way straight to the top of  the list is luffy punching a celestial  dragon this is the moment that defines  luffy as the upstart who's not afraid of  anyone not least of those undeservedly  holding on to positions of great power  and influence it also shows how deeply  luffy cares for his friends how little  he cares for an established order that  discriminates against certain people and  how he has his own strong sense of  justice the slow walk up the stairs of  the auction house where the snively  saint chalos has just shot hachi simply  for fun is now iconic so is the  dangerous look in luffy's eyes before he  unleashes that swinging punch smack dab  into noble's face in the one piece  universe the celestial dragons are  portrayed as weak yet powerful  privileged yet irresponsible cruel and  lacking compassion to see one of their  worst get his just desserts is such  sweet satisfaction that it's luffy who  enforces this much needed justice makes  him that much more badass  and that's it for the top 10 badass  luffy moments in one piece if you like  this video you know what to do next  don't you press the like button and  share the video with your friends you  can also subscribe to my channel vinnie  tube for more one piece and anime  related top 10s and videos there's  plenty to choose from share your  thoughts in the comments below and i'll  see you in the next video  [Music]  you

